e\":\"Neem Oil\",\"dosage\":\"10ml per liter\",\"frequency\":\"Every 7-10 days\",\"note\":\"Apply after petal fall, never mix with sulfur.\"}]','[\"Rake up and destroy fallen leaves in autumn\",\"Prune trees to open the canopy for better air circulation and sunlight\",\"Plant scab-resistant varieties (e.g., Liberty, Honeycrisp)\"]'),(32,92.9,'C:/uploads/download.webp','Healthy','2026-04-08 05:04:10.000000','No action needed. Keep maintaining current care.',1,'Optimal soil nutrients and climate conditions maintained.','[{\"name\":\"Balanced NPK Fertilizer (19:19:19)\",\"dosage\":\"5g per liter of water\",\"frequency\":\"Every 15 days during growth\",\"note\":\"Adjust based on soil test results.\"},{\"name\":\"Micronutrient Mix (Zn, Fe, Mn, B)\",\"dosage\":\"As per soil test recommendations\",\"frequency\":\"Once every 2 months\",\"note\":\"Apply only if deficiency is confirmed through testing.\"}]','[{\"name\":\"Compost Application\",\"dosage\":\"2-3 kg per square meter\",\"frequency\":\"Every 3-4 months\",\"note\":\"Maintains soil health and beneficial microbes.\"},{\"name\":\"Organic Mulch\",\"dosage\":\"5-7 cm layer around plants\",\"frequency\":\"Replenish as needed\",\"note\":\"Conserves moisture and suppresses weeds naturally.\"},{\"name\":\"Seaweed Extract\",\"dosage\":\"2ml per liter of water\",\"frequency\":\"Monthly foliar spray\",\"note\":\"Boosts plant immunity and stress tolerance.\"}]','[\"Continue regular monitoring for early disease detection\",\"Maintain proper watering schedule based on crop needs\",\"Keep balanced nutrition through soil testing every 6 months\",\"Practice integrated pest management (IPM)\",\"Maintain soil pH between 6.0-7.0 for most crops\",\"Ensure good drainage to prevent waterlogging\",\"Rotate crops annually to prevent soil depletion\",\"Keep farm records for better decision making\"]'),(33,93.21,'C:/uploads/download (1).webp','Rice Blast','2026-04-08 05:04:58.000000','Manage water levels closely and avoid excessive nitrogen application.',1,'Fungal disease caused by Magnaporthe oryzae under high humidity and excessive nitrogen.','[{\"name\":\"Tricyclazole 75% WP\",\"dosage\":\"0.6g per liter\",\"frequency\":\"At heading stage\",\"note\":\"Specifically targets rice blast.\"},{\"name\":\"Isoprothiolane 40% EC\",\"dosage\":\"1.5ml per liter\",\"frequency\":\"Early infection stage\",\"note\":\"Systemic action against blast.\"}]','[{\"name\":\"Bacillus subtilis Biofungicide\",\"dosage\":\"2-3ml per liter\",\"frequency\":\"Every 10 dates\",\"note\":\"Competitive inhibition of the blast fungus.\"},{\"name\":\"Silicon soil amendments\",\"dosage\":\"As per package\",\"frequency\":\"Applied at planting\",\"note\":\"Strengthens plant cell walls against fungal penetration.\"}]','[\"Burn or plow under infected crop residues\",\"Avoid excessive nitrogen fertilization\",\"Use resistant seed varieties\",\"Maintain proper flood levels in paddies\"]'),(34,96.74,'C:/uploads/download (1).webp','Tomato Early Blight','2026-04-10 05:20:53.000000','Remove lower affected leaves, improve air flow, and apply fungicide.',1,'Fungal disease caused by Alternaria solani, thriving in warm, humid weather.','[{\"name\":\"Chlorothalonil 75% WP\",\"dosage\":\"2g per liter of water\",\"frequency\":\"Every 7-10 days\",\"note\":\"Preventative fungicide, do not apply during extreme heat.\"},{\"name\":\"Mancozeb 75% WP\",\"dosage\":\"2.5g per liter of water\",\"frequency\":\"Every 7-10 days\",\"note\":\"Broad-spectrum contact fungicide.\"}]','[{\"name\":\"Copper Fungicide\",\"dosage\":\"2-3 ml per liter of water\",\"frequency\":\"Weekly\",\"note\":\"Organic copper-based sprays are effective early on.\"},{\"name\":\"Compost Tea\",\"dosage\":\"Dilute 1:5 with water\",\"frequency\":\"Every 5-7 days\",\"note\":\"Improves plant immunity and coats leaves with beneficial microbes.\"}]','[\"Rotate crops (do not plant tomatoes in the same spot for 3-4 years)\",\"Provide adequate spacing for air circulation\",\"Mulch around the base of the plant to prevent soil splash\",\"Stake or cage plants to keep foliage off the ground\"]'),(35,96.04,'C:/uploads/download (1).webp','Blight','2026-04-10 06:05:03.000000','Remove affected plants. Rotate crops next season.',1,'Bacterial infection often spread by wind and rain in early spring.','[{\"name\":\"Copper Hydroxide 77% WP\",\"dosage\":\"3g per liter of water\",\"frequency\":\"Every 7-10 days\",\"note\":\"Protective fungicide. Wear mask and gloves during application.\"},{\"name\":\"Streptomycin Sulfate (for bacterial blight)\",\"dosage\":\"200 ppm solution\",\"frequency\":\"Every 5 days during infection\",\"note\":\"Antibiotic. Use only when necessary. PHI: 14 days.\"},{\"name\":\"Chlorothalonil 75% WP\",\"dosage\":\"2g per liter of water\",\"frequency\":\"Every 10 days\",\"note\":\"Broad-spectrum. Do not mix with other pesticides.\"},{\"name\":\"Mancozeb 75% WP (Preventive)\",\"dosage\":\"2.5g per liter of water\",\"frequency\":\"Every 10-14 days\",\"note\":\"Start before disease appears. PHI: 7 days.\"}]','[{\"name\":\"Copper-Based Organic Bactericide\",\"dosage\":\"2-3g per liter of water\",\"frequency\":\"Every 5-7 days\",\"note\":\"OMRI listed. Apply preventively before disease appears.\"},{\"name\":\"Bacillus subtilis Biofungicide\",\"dosage\":\"As per manufacturer (typically 2ml/L)\",\"frequency\":\"Every 7-10 days\",\"note\":\"Beneficial bacteria. Safe for beneficial insects.\"},{\"name\":\"Compost Tea\",\"dosage\":\"Dilute 1:5 with water\",\"frequency\":\"Weekly as foliar spray\",\"note\":\"Boosts plant immunity. Use well-aerated compost tea only.\"}]','[\"Use only certified disease-free seeds and transplants\",\"Practice 3-4 year crop rotation with non-host crops\",\"Avoid working with plants when foliage is wet\",\"Sanitize all tools with 10% bleach solution between plants\",\"Remove and destroy volunteer plants immediately\",\"Apply organic mulch to prevent soil splash onto leaves\",\"Maintain proper plant nutrition with balanced fertilizers\",\"Install drip irrigation to keep foliage dry\",\"Remove crop residues immediately after harvest\"]'),(36,99.72,'C:/uploads/Screenshot 2026-05-22 093441.png','Apple Scab','2026-05-22 04:06:00.000000','Apply protective fungicide sprays in early spring.',1,'Venturia inaequalis fungi overwintering in fallen leaves.','[{\"name\":\"Captan 50% WP\",\"dosage\":\"2.5g per liter\",\"frequency\":\"Every 7-14 days\",\"note\":\"Start at green tip stage, do not use with oils.\"},{\"name\":\"Myclobutanil\",\"dosage\":\"0.5g per liter\",\"frequency\":\"Post-infection within 96 hours\",\"note\":\"Has strong curative properties.\"}]','[{\"name\":\"Liquid Lime-Sulfur\",\"dosage\":\"Follow specific label for dormancy/green tip\",\"frequency\":\"Early spring\",\"note\":\"Applying at green tip stage significantly reduces primary infection.\"},{\"name\":\"Neem Oil\",\"dosage\":\"10ml per liter\",\"frequency\":\"Every 7-10 days\",\"note\":\"Apply after petal fall, never mix with sulfur.\"}]','[\"Rake up and destroy fallen leaves in autumn\",\"Prune trees to open the canopy for better air circulation and sunlight\",\"Plant scab-resistant varieties (e.g., Liberty, Honeycrisp)\"]'),(37,94.72,'C:/uploads/Screenshot 2026-05-22 093441.png','Rice Blast','2026-05-22 04:22:13.000000','Manage water levels closely and avoid excessive nitrogen application.',1,'Fungal disease caused by Magnaporthe oryzae under high humidity and excessive nitrogen.','[{\"name\":\"Tricyclazole 75% WP\",\"dosage\":\"0.6g per liter\",\"frequency\":\"At heading stage\",\"note\":\"Specifically targets rice blast.\"},{\"name\":\"Isoprothiolane 40% EC\",\"dosage\":\"1.5ml per liter\",\"frequency\":\"Early infection stage\",\"note\":\"Systemic action against blast.\"}]','[{\"name\":\"Bacillus subtilis Biofungicide\",\"dosage\":\"2-3ml per liter\",\"frequency\":\"Every 10 dates\",\"note\":\"Competitive inhibition of the blast fungus.\"},{\"name\":\"Silicon soil amendments\",\"dosage\":\"As per package\",\"frequency\":\"Applied at planting\",\"note\":\"Strengthens plant cell walls against fungal penetration.\"}]','[\"Burn or plow under infected crop residues\",\"Avoid excessive nitrogen fertilization\",\"Use resistant seed varieties\",\"Maintain proper flood levels in paddies\"]');
